# Redirect map for the risanb.com / blog.risanb.com split.
#
# Read by Cloudflare Workers static assets at deploy time (dist/_redirects), and
# parsed by scripts/check-site.mjs which fails the build if a rule would shadow a
# page the site actually serves, or if an indexed URL is left uncovered.
#
# 301 is stated explicitly on every line. The platform defaults to 302 when the
# status is omitted, and a 302 does NOT transfer ranking the way a 301 does --
# which is the entire point of this file.
#
# ORDER: static rules first, then the single splat rule last. Cloudflare
# documents that static redirects must precede dynamic ones. The rules below are
# disjoint so either order resolves identically today, but precedence is applied
# top-down and a future rule could quietly become unreachable -- so keep the
# `/blog/*` splat at the bottom of this file.
#
# These redirects are applied by the static-assets layer. They are SKIPPED for
# any request a Worker script handles, which is why wrangler.jsonc deliberately
# defines no `main` script and no `run_worker_first`.
#
# Derived from the 250 URLs in https://risanb.com/sitemap.xml (captured 2026-09-21,
# snapshotted in scripts/legacy-urls.txt). Each is either served by the new
# build or redirected here; none is dropped.
#
#   /categories/<blog-term>/ -> blog.risanb.com/...       (4 rules)
#   /tags/<blog-term>/       -> blog.risanb.com/...       (25 rules)
#   /blog/*                  -> blog.risanb.com/:splat    (143 URLs, 1 rule)
#
# Code posts keep /code/:slug/ unchanged, so no technical post redirects at all.

# --- blog-only categories (code keeps log, snippet, tutorial) ---------------

/categories/journal/  https://blog.risanb.com/categories/journal/  301
/categories/photos/  https://blog.risanb.com/categories/photos/  301
/categories/travel/  https://blog.risanb.com/categories/travel/  301
/categories/writing/  https://blog.risanb.com/categories/writing/  301

